{"Problem": "As shown in the figure, there is a sequence of curves \( P_{0}, P_{1}, P_{2}, \ldots \). It is known that \( P_{0} \) is an equilateral triangle with an area of 1. \( P_{k+1} \) is obtained from \( P_{k} \) by the following operation: Each side of \( P_{k} \) is divided into three equal parts, and on the middle segment of each side, an equilateral triangle is constructed externally, then the middle segments are removed \((k = 0, 1, 2, \ldots)\). Let \( S_{n} \) represent the area of the figure enclosed by the curve \( P_{n} \).

(1) Find the general term formula for the sequence \{S_{n}\}.
(2) Compute \lim_{n \rightarrow \infty} S_{n}\.", "Step 3": "[CONDITION] Area of small triangle added at stage \( n-1 \) is \( \frac{1}{9^{n-1}} \). [PROCESS] Calculate total area increase from \( P_{n-1} \) to \( P_n \): \( \Delta S_n = a_{n-1} \cdot \frac{1}{9^{n-1}} = 3 \cdot 4^{n-2} \cdot \frac{1}{9^{n-1}} \). [CONCLUSION] \( \Delta S_n = 3 \cdot 4^{n-2} \cdot \frac{1}{9^{n-1}} \)"}

{"Problem": "As shown in the figure, there is a sequence of curves \( P_{0}, P_{1}, P_{2}, \ldots \). It is known that \( P_{0} \) is an equilateral triangle with an area of 1. \( P_{k+1} \) is obtained from \( P_{k} \) by the following operation: Each side of \( P_{k} \) is divided into three equal parts, and on the middle segment of each side, an equilateral triangle is constructed externally, then the middle segments are removed \((k = 0, 1, 2, \ldots)\). Let \( S_{n} \) represent the area of the figure enclosed by the curve \( P_{n} \).

(1) Find the general term formula for the sequence \{S_{n}\}.
(2) Compute \lim_{n \rightarrow \infty} S_{n}\.", "Step 4": "[CONDITION] Area increase from \( P_{n-1} \) to \( P_n \) is known. [PROCESS] Formulate recursive area formula: \( S_n = S_{n-1} + \Delta S_n \). [CONCLUSION] \( S_n = S_{n-1} + \frac{3}{4} \left(\frac{4}{9}\right)^{n-1} \)"}

